 "audit": "Six cases carry thousands of mutations and several others >100 (hypermutators; one has 15,731), which would create spurious gene associations; I excluded cases with >100 mutations and cases with missing/Unknown diagnosis. Diagnosis labels are fragmented and overlapping (e.g. Glioma malignant vs Glioblastoma vs Astrocytoma NOS; several rhabdomyosarcoma labels; NOS/uncertain labels), so 'other tumors' comparison groups are impure and small groups give unstable estimates. Many tests (232) were run so I used Bonferroni-adjusted one-sided Fisher tests and kept only adjusted p<0.1. Some hits (e.g. NOTCH2 in embryonal RMS, MED12 in ependymoma, NF2 in pilocytic astrocytoma) are not clearly in the literature and could reflect pooling/site/batch or long-gene passenger effects; I did not find ten robust novel findings and did not inflate the list to meet that request. Expected frequencies are shrunk slightly from observed to account for winner's curse.",
 "methods": "Removed cases with >100 non-synonymous mutations and missing/Unknown diagnoses (1605 cases kept). Counted cases mutated per gene per diagnosis (diagnoses n>=8, genes mutated in >=3 cases, >=3 in the diagnosis), one-sided Fisher exact test versus all other kept cases, Bonferroni over 232 tests. Reported hits with adjusted p<0.1 and observed frequency >=5%; probabilities scaled by significance, capped for non-established findings; established flag from prior knowledge."
}